ttychatter.mailbot walkthrough
==============================

This walkthrough assumes:

    mailbot user:        r94
    mailbot binary:      /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot
    ttychatter binary:   /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.python
    config file:         /home/r94/.config/ttychatter/mailbot/config
    session directory:   /home/r94/.local/share/ttychatter/openrouter/sessions
    model cache:         /home/r94/.config/ttychatter/openrouter/models-cache.json

Install files
-------------

    install -m 0755 ttychatter.mailbot /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot
    install -m 0644 ttychatter.mailbot.1 /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot.1

For a system manpage install:

    doas install -m 0644 ttychatter.mailbot.1 /usr/local/share/man/man1/ttychatter.mailbot.1

Minimum config
--------------

Create /home/r94/.config/ttychatter/mailbot/config:

    IMAP_HOST=localhost
    IMAP_PORT=993
    IMAP_SSL=1
    IMAP_USER=r94
    IMAP_MAILBOX=INBOX

    SEND_METHOD=sendmail
    SENDMAIL=/usr/sbin/sendmail

    MAIL_FROM=ttychatter@localhost
    ALLOWED_FROM=you@example.org

    SUBJECT_PREFIX=tc
    CONFIG_SUBJECT_TOKEN=CONFIG
    MODELS_SUBJECT_TOKEN=MODELS
    COMMAND_SUBJECT_TOKEN=CMD
    MAILBOT_SUBJECT_TOKEN=MAILBOT

    TTYCHATTER_COMMAND=/usr/local/bin/python3 /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.python
    SESSION_DIR=/home/r94/.local/share/ttychatter/openrouter/sessions
    ATTACHMENT_DIR=/home/r94/.local/share/ttychatter/openrouter/attachments
    MODEL_CACHE_FILE=/home/r94/.config/ttychatter/openrouter/models-cache.json

    MAILBOT_MANPAGE_FILE=/home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot.1

Keep it private:

    chmod 600 /home/r94/.config/ttychatter/mailbot/config

Password source
---------------

Plaintext local password, protected by file mode:

    IMAP_PASSWORD=your-imap-password

Encrypted password file:

    /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --set-imap-password --gpg

Then the config should contain:

    IMAP_PASSWORD_GPG_FILE=/home/r94/.config/ttychatter/mailbot/imap-password.gpg

A cron or daemon process can decrypt that file only if gpg-agent can unlock it
without an interactive prompt. If not, use a protected plaintext IMAP_PASSWORD
line, TTYCHATTER_IMAP_PASSWORD in the service environment, or a local secret
manager appropriate to the host.

Initial diagnostics
-------------------

Run as the same user that will run the cron or daemon:

    su -l r94
    /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --version
    /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --config
    /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --doctor
    /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --list-candidates
    /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --once --dry-run

If --config shows the wrong CONFIG_FILE, fix the command line or environment
before debugging IMAP, GPG, or mail syntax.

0.4 mail syntax
---------------

Control subjects are bare:

    tc:CONFIG
    tc:MODELS
    tc:CMD
    tc:help
    tc:sessions
    tc:manpage
    tc:search TEXT

Chat sessions are braced:

    tc:{session-name}
    tc:{new}

tc:{new} passes no session argument to ttychatter.python. ttychatter.python
therefore creates its regular default name, such as:

    session-2026-05-30-01-02-03

Legacy subjects still accepted
------------------------------

The mailbot still accepts these older control subjects:

    tc:{CONFIG}
    tc:{MAILBOT}
    tc:{MAILBOT:command args}

They are compatibility aliases. Use the bare 0.4 subjects for new mail.

Send a test chat
----------------

From an allowed sender, send:

    Subject: tc:{mailbot-test}

    Say one sentence confirming this mailbot test.

Then run:

    /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --once

The reply should include:

    ttychatter.mailbot success
    session: mailbot-test

Start a new unnamed chat
------------------------

Send:

    Subject: tc:{new}

    Start a fresh session and summarize what this mail is testing.

The mailbot passes no session name to ttychatter.python. The reply should show
the session name detected from ttychatter's loopback stderr when available.

Request config by email
-----------------------

Send:

    Subject: tc:CONFIG

With no config attachment, the reply attaches:

    ttychatter-mailbot-config.txt

Plaintext IMAP_PASSWORD and SMTP_PASSWORD values are redacted.

To update config by email, edit that attachment and send it back with the same
subject:

    Subject: tc:CONFIG

The mailbot writes a timestamped backup before replacing the config. Dry-run
never writes the config.

Refresh model cache by email
----------------------------

Send:

    Subject: tc:MODELS

The mailbot runs:

    ttychatter.python --update-models

Then it attaches the resulting cache as:

    models-cache.json

If ttychatter output reports:

    updated model cache: /path/to/models-cache.json

the mailbot uses that path. Otherwise it falls back to MODEL_CACHE_FILE.

List models without refreshing cache
------------------------------------

Use model-list, list-models, models-list, show-models, or models with flags for a ttychatter --models query:

    Subject: tc:model-list --all --sort context

or put the arguments in the body:

    Subject: tc:model-list

    --all --sort context

Router listing is similar:

    Subject: tc:routers --model-type chat --require-tokens

List sessions by email
----------------------

Send:

    Subject: tc:sessions

The reply lists session logs newest first, with modified time, byte count, line
count, and head/tail previews. Tune output with:

    SESSION_LIST_HEAD_LINES=3
    SESSION_LIST_TAIL_LINES=3
    SESSION_LIST_MAX_SESSIONS=50
    SESSION_PREVIEW_LINE_CHARS=220

Search sessions by email
------------------------

Direct subject:

    Subject: tc:search gpg-agent

Body argument form:

    Subject: tc:search

    gpg-agent

Single-session search:

    Subject: tc:search-session mailbot-test gpg-agent

Rename a session by email
-------------------------

Send:

    Subject: tc:rename-session old-name new-name

Dry-run prints what would happen and does not rename.

Fetch the mailbot manpage by email
----------------------------------

Send:

    Subject: tc:manpage

Aliases:

    tc:manual
    tc:get-manpage
    tc:fetch-manpage

The reply attaches ttychatter.mailbot.1. The mailbot uses the first readable
external manpage it finds, falling back to its embedded manpage.

Use tc:CMD for body-line commands
---------------------------------

Send:

    Subject: tc:CMD

    sessions

or:

    Subject: tc:CMD

    search mailbot-test

This is useful when a command is easier to write in the body than in the
subject.

Other safe commands
-------------------

Examples:

    tc:ttydoctor
    tc:ttyconfig
    tc:credits
    tc:favorites
    tc:favorite-model openai/gpt-5
    tc:unfavorite-model openai/gpt-5
    tc:test-model openai/gpt-5
    tc:show-memory mailbot-test
    tc:clear-memory mailbot-test
    tc:tty-set DEFAULT_MODEL openai/gpt-5
    tc:tty-unset DEFAULT_MODEL

tty-set refuses OPENROUTER_API_KEY and API_KEY by email. Set secrets locally.

Cron example
------------

Install the cron job in r94's crontab, not root's, unless root is the intended
mailbot account.

    SHELL=/bin/sh
    HOME=/home/r94
    PATH=/home/r94/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin
    MAILTO=""

    */2 * * * * -s /usr/local/bin/python3 /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --config-file /home/r94/.config/ttychatter/mailbot/config --once >>/home/r94/.local/share/ttychatter/mailbot.log 2>&1

On OpenBSD, -s prevents overlapping runs. Invoking the mailbot through the
absolute Python path avoids cron PATH failures from #!/usr/bin/env python3.

Check the log:

    tail -f /home/r94/.local/share/ttychatter/mailbot.log

Troubleshooting checklist
-------------------------

1. Wrong user or wrong config:

       ttychatter.mailbot --config
       ttychatter.mailbot --doctor

   Confirm PROCESS_USER, HOME, and CONFIG_FILE.

2. No candidate messages:

       ttychatter.mailbot --list-candidates

   Look for sender allowlist failures or subject syntax failures.

3. Subject syntax failures:

       control: tc:CONFIG, tc:MODELS, tc:CMD, tc:command args
       chat:    tc:{session-name}, tc:{new}

4. GPG failure:

       export GPG_TTY=$(tty)
       gpgconf --launch gpg-agent
       gpg-connect-agent updatestartuptty /bye
       gpg --decrypt ~/.config/ttychatter/mailbot/imap-password.gpg >/dev/null

5. Cron says env cannot find python3:

       use /usr/local/bin/python3 /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot
       set TTYCHATTER_COMMAND=/usr/local/bin/python3 /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.python

6. IMAP LOGIN command BAD:

       check IMAP_USER, password source, CR/LF in passwords, and wrong HOME.
